 \"胺碘酮 exerts measurable effects on key cardiovascular hemodynamic indicators, including cardiac index, stroke volume (搏出量), and pulmonary capillary wedge pressure (PCWP). In patients with impaired left ventricular function, intravenous administration of 胺碘酮 (5 mg/kg) resulted in reduced heart rate, cardiac index, and stroke volume within one hour—changes not attributable to peripheral vascular resistance. Two patients with severely compromised hemodynamics experienced blood pressure drops, underscoring the need for hemodynamic monitoring during therapy. These findings suggest that while 胺碘酮 is effective for arrhythmia control, it may depress cardiac output in vulnerable populations, requiring cautious use in heart failure patients [Data: Relationships (4022, 4048, 4050)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"胺碘酮 induces thyroid-related biochemical changes\",\n            \"explanation\": \"胺碘酮 influences thyroid hormone metabolism, notably decreasing serum triiodothyronine (T3, 三碘甲腺原氨酸) levels while increasing thyroxine (T4). Although these changes often remain within normal ranges, the level of reverse T3 (rT3) correlates strongly with both therapeutic efficacy and toxicity of 胺碘酮. Dynamic monitoring of rT3 and SHBG (sex hormone-binding globulin) has been proposed as a clinically useful strategy for assessing long-term treatment outcomes and adverse effects. However, rT3 levels can also be elevated in non-thyroidal illnesses like myocardial infarction or liver cirrhosis, limiting specificity. Thus, while thyroid function tests provide valuable insights, they must be interpreted in clinical context [Data: Relationships (4026, 4033)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Pulmonary and autoimmune markers are affected by 胺碘酮\",\n            \"explanation\": \"胺碘酮 is associated with pulmonary toxicity, including interstitial pneumonitis and fibrosis, which may involve autoimmune mechanisms. Clinical evidence reports elevated immunoglobulins and positive antinuclear antibodies (抗核抗体) at titers of 1:200 in affected patients, suggesting an autoimmune component to lung injury—though direct drug toxicity cannot be ruled out. Radiological changes detectable via X光检查 (X-ray imaging) are part of the diagnostic workup for suspected amiodarone-induced lung disease. Given the severity of potential pulmonary complications (occurring in ~0.5% of patients), clinicians are advised to monitor respiratory symptoms, inflammatory markers, and imaging findings during long-term therapy [Data: Relationships (4031, 4049)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Myocardial and electrocardiographic effects correlate with tissue concentrations\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The electrophysiological impact of 胺碘酮, particularly QTc interval prolongation, demonstrates a strong linear correlation with both blood and myocardial concentrations (r=0.92 and r=0.96, respectively). Long-term oral use increases QTc by an average of 18.5%, proportional to dose escalation. This relationship supports using QTc changes as a surrogate marker for drug accumulation in cardiac tissue. While QTc prolongation under 30% is generally not associated with severe arrhythmias, the drug’s effect on repolarization necessitates ECG surveillance, especially when combined with other QT-prolonging agents. Notably, other ECG changes include PR prolongation, T-wave notching, prominent U waves, and occasional ST depression [Data: Relationships (4047)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"胺碘酮 interacts with other antiarrhythmic drugs, including 安他唑啉\",\n            \"explanation\": \"胺碘酮 exhibits clinically significant pharmacodynamic and pharmacokinetic interactions with several antiarrhythmic agents, particularly 安他唑啉. Co-administration is reported to enhance therapeutic efficacy in refractory arrhythmias, but also increases the risk of excessive QT prolongation and torsades de pointes. The interaction with procainamide (普鲁